WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:30.000
{IF YOU ARE SEEING THIS, YOUR PLAYER IS NOT RENDERING THE SUBTITLES PROPERLY. PLEASE REFER TO http://saizen-fansubs.com/?section=playback FOR THE INTENDED PLAYBACK.}

00:00:24.880 --> 00:00:25.820
I-It's useless.

00:00:25.820 --> 00:00:26.710
I-It's useless.

00:00:27.240 --> 00:00:30.520
After all, with just one day of trying to throw at that spot...

00:00:30.520 --> 00:00:35.130
I won't be able to match up to Sanchez's powerful control at all!

00:00:37.760 --> 00:00:40.140
<i>If you're so scared of having your pitches hit,</i>

00:00:40.140 --> 00:00:42.220
<i>volunteer to drop down to the Minors yourself!</i>

00:00:42.770 --> 00:00:44.640
<i>You're too naive!</i>

00:00:53.200 --> 00:00:55.780
Get hit and go to the Minors, huh?

00:00:55.780 --> 00:00:59.130
If I don't have enough power, then it can't be helped, I guess.

00:02:56.970 --> 00:02:59.110
Hi! Is everyone in a good mood?

00:02:59.620 --> 00:03:04.950
To each and every Salmons fan who has loved the Salmons since they were small...

00:03:05.390 --> 00:03:08.910
Today as usual, I, Mathew Taylor will be announcing for you!

00:03:09.390 --> 00:03:13.580
In today's exhibition game they play the power-hitting Dallas Elephants!

00:03:13.580 --> 00:03:18.300
Facing them is our own Salmons, whose starting pitcher is - Oh, is that true? A Japanese player!

00:03:18.300 --> 00:03:23.500
Having just passed the tryouts, it's Goro Shigeno!

00:03:38.530 --> 00:03:44.530
<i>Even the scale of the ceremony and the mood of the audience is on a different level from Japan.</i>

00:03:47.420 --> 00:03:51.070
<i>Will my pitching work against these guys?</i>

00:03:51.070 --> 00:03:54.060
<i>Am I just going to be exposed as a fraud and be publicly humiliated?</i>

00:03:54.970 --> 00:03:56.440
<i>Anyway,</i>

00:03:56.440 --> 00:03:58.630
<i>I'll do what I can!</i>

00:04:09.340 --> 00:04:10.460
Strike!

00:04:13.990 --> 00:04:17.560
<i>I heard that he had just passed the tryouts, but...</i>

00:04:18.010 --> 00:04:19.270
<i>Oh?</i>

00:04:19.270 --> 00:04:21.490
<i>I thought he was going to be paralyzed due to nerves, but...</i>

00:04:22.690 --> 00:04:25.360
<i>he isn't pitching half bad.</i>

00:04:30.670 --> 00:04:32.330
Strike two!

00:04:33.350 --> 00:04:36.750
Coach, this might actually go unexpectedly well.

00:04:40.330 --> 00:04:41.870
<i>What are you saying!?</i>

00:04:41.870 --> 00:04:44.320
<i>You're going to use Shigeno as the starting pitcher in the exhibition game?</i>

00:04:44.320 --> 00:04:46.640
<i>Are you serious, Assistant General Manager?</i>

00:04:47.110 --> 00:04:51.590
<i>Letting a rookie, who just passed the tryouts, join up with the Majors camp is unheard of!</i>

00:04:51.590 --> 00:04:53.520
<i>This kind of special treatment has never been done up till now!</i>

00:04:54.180 --> 00:04:55.850
<i>It's the owner's idea.</i>

00:04:56.870 --> 00:04:58.000
<i>The owner's?</i>

00:04:58.780 --> 00:05:04.720
<i>These days, we can't ignore the ability to attract fans and the economic benefits that Japanese players bring.</i>

00:05:04.720 --> 00:05:09.510
<i>If it's possible, we want to bring in Japanese tourists to the Salmons too.</i>

00:05:09.510 --> 00:05:10.700
<i>That's the idea.</i>

00:05:11.080 --> 00:05:15.460
<i>But, that's only the case for Japanese stars who are former top players.</i>

00:05:15.460 --> 00:05:18.160
<i>As Shigeno is right now, he doesn't have the ability to attract fans, and...</i>

00:05:18.160 --> 00:05:20.280
<i>I strongly recommended him.</i>

00:05:22.740 --> 00:05:26.510
<i>I don't believe he'll become a usable "weapon" immediately of course.</i>

00:05:27.260 --> 00:05:29.090
<i>He was easily hit by Bolton.</i>

00:05:31.420 --> 00:05:36.200
<i>And the difference in power in his duel with Sanchez was evident too, from what I've heard.</i>

00:05:36.530 --> 00:05:39.940
<i>However, there's some sort of aura about him.</i>

00:05:39.940 --> 00:05:41.640
<i>In the end, it's just my intuition, but...</i>

00:05:41.640 --> 00:05:45.280
<i>he's got the same scent as many star players had when they were young.</i>

00:05:45.280 --> 00:05:50.200
<i>E-Even with saying that, with such a reckless plan, that itself will be destroyed!</i>

00:05:50.200 --> 00:05:53.730
<i>The majority of rookies start in the Minors.</i>

00:05:52.430 --> 00:05:53.730
<i>Gary-kun.</i>

00:05:53.730 --> 00:05:54.560
<i>Yes?</i>

00:05:55.660 --> 00:06:01.500
<i>Have you seen any idiots coming to take the tryouts with just a fastball these days?</i>

00:06:07.370 --> 00:06:08.310
<i>In other words,</i>

00:06:08.310 --> 00:06:13.850
<i>this is a man who has a lot of confidence and pride, and has crossed the sea to come here.</i>

00:06:13.850 --> 00:06:15.810
<i>That kind of person...</i>

00:06:18.840 --> 00:06:20.230
Strike out!

00:06:20.230 --> 00:06:22.150
All right!

00:06:24.150 --> 00:06:29.070
<i>That kind of person isn't the type to get crushed by the wall that is the Majors so easily.</i>

00:06:29.070 --> 00:06:31.340
A wall, huh?

00:06:35.250 --> 00:06:36.620
Strike out!

00:06:38.640 --> 00:06:40.120
Strike out!

00:06:40.540 --> 00:06:41.580
<i>Okay!</i>

00:06:42.050 --> 00:06:43.000
<i>Yeah!</i>

00:06:43.000 --> 00:06:45.920
The game begins promisingly.

00:06:49.170 --> 00:06:52.300
I somehow managed to suppress them all in the first inning.

00:06:53.480 --> 00:06:58.100
We underestimated him because we thought he was a rookie, but he can throw quite the fastball.

00:06:58.100 --> 00:06:59.140
Be careful.

00:07:03.910 --> 00:07:05.320
Strike out!

00:07:06.560 --> 00:07:07.650
Strike out!

00:07:11.560 --> 00:07:12.490
Out!

00:07:13.600 --> 00:07:15.730
So our team was retired in order too.

00:07:15.730 --> 00:07:19.160
Our opponents really aren't making it easy for us either, huh?

00:07:19.160 --> 00:07:23.080
Now batting, number 7, Guererra!

00:07:23.650 --> 00:07:26.150
Guererra is the Elephants' main slugger.

00:07:26.150 --> 00:07:27.710
He was the home run king last year.

00:07:27.710 --> 00:07:30.680
Oh, he's a dangerous opponent, huh?

00:07:30.680 --> 00:07:32.940
We've got to avoid giving up the first runs.

00:07:32.940 --> 00:07:34.680
Whatever the case is, don't get sucked in.

00:07:37.880 --> 00:07:38.600
Play!

00:07:38.600 --> 00:07:41.160
<i>You're saying I'm going to get sucked in?</i>

00:07:41.160 --> 00:07:42.520
<i>Don't joke around!</i>

00:07:45.990 --> 00:07:47.440
Strike!

00:07:49.090 --> 00:07:50.900
Strike two!

00:07:55.000 --> 00:07:56.450
<i>The battle starts on the next pitch...</i>

00:08:00.820 --> 00:08:02.310
Strike out!

00:08:04.380 --> 00:08:05.710
<i>He let it by?</i>

00:08:05.710 --> 00:08:06.680
All right!

00:08:07.430 --> 00:08:11.140
<i>So Guererra is just going to wait and conduct research his first at-bat too.</i>

00:08:11.140 --> 00:08:12.590
<i>And what's up with that kid?</i>

00:08:13.250 --> 00:08:16.260
<i>Even when someone like Guererra is facing him, he's not faltering in the least.</i>

00:08:16.260 --> 00:08:19.510
<i>Although nothing else stands out, that courage of his is really something.</i>

00:08:25.010 --> 00:08:26.540
Strike out!

00:08:31.570 --> 00:08:32.810
<i>All right!</i>

00:08:34.130 --> 00:08:35.000
Out!

00:08:36.640 --> 00:08:39.950
I can't believe you complained and said you couldn't be the starting pitcher.

00:08:39.950 --> 00:08:42.120
Let's forget about that.

00:08:43.470 --> 00:08:46.080
<i>The Majors is like this, huh?</i>

00:08:46.540 --> 00:08:50.500
<i>There was something wrong with me being scared before the fight began.</i>

00:09:10.570 --> 00:09:12.480
Go, Fox!

00:09:22.510 --> 00:09:23.620
Out!

00:09:23.620 --> 00:09:25.970
Oh no!

00:09:26.960 --> 00:09:27.760
Damn!

00:09:32.200 --> 00:09:33.930
Don't mind, don't mind.

00:09:33.930 --> 00:09:35.380
Don't get so angry.

00:09:44.480 --> 00:09:46.060
Strike out!

00:09:48.700 --> 00:09:51.650
I guess the Majors really are the Majors after all.

00:09:51.650 --> 00:09:55.940
Doesn't he understand that he's the pitcher?

00:09:59.600 --> 00:10:01.030
Strike out!

00:10:30.600 --> 00:10:33.060
Leading by two runs in the top half of the fifth inning...

00:10:33.060 --> 00:10:36.970
To think that the Japanese rookie would be able to so steadily suppress them this far.

00:10:37.570 --> 00:10:40.530
I really thought it was absurd to have Shigeno as the starting pitcher, but...

00:10:41.290 --> 00:10:44.450
the owner's decision wasn't wrong.

00:10:45.890 --> 00:10:47.150
Well, I'm not so sure about that.

00:10:47.150 --> 00:10:48.370
Well, I'm not so sure about that.

00:10:56.220 --> 00:11:01.250
This is a free fansub.

00:10:56.220 --> 00:11:01.250
Not for sale or rent.

00:11:06.690 --> 00:11:07.460
Play!

00:11:08.560 --> 00:11:12.480
You've returned, Mr. Home Run King-san.

00:11:12.980 --> 00:11:14.650
<i>No matter how many times you come up...</i>

00:11:15.950 --> 00:11:17.320
<i>I won't let you hit!</i>

00:11:22.630 --> 00:11:23.820
This is bad!

00:11:26.740 --> 00:11:28.230
No way...

00:11:28.230 --> 00:11:29.740
On the first pitch...

00:11:34.920 --> 00:11:37.380
<i>If it wasn't this way, it wouldn't be interesting.</i>

00:11:37.380 --> 00:11:40.550
<i>Then there wouldn't be any reason for me to challenge the Majors.</i>

00:11:43.330 --> 00:11:45.430
<i>The real battle starts now.</i>

00:11:52.690 --> 00:11:53.760
Damn!

00:11:53.760 --> 00:11:55.480
He hit it really well!

00:12:18.960 --> 00:12:23.260
<i>It seems like they've gradually figured out that Shigeno has only fastballs.</i>

00:12:24.570 --> 00:12:28.270
Did they get pumped up from Guererra's home run, perhaps?

00:12:28.270 --> 00:12:29.640
What should we do?

00:12:30.130 --> 00:12:31.260
Well then, I suppose I'll go and warm up.

00:12:31.260 --> 00:12:32.480
Well then, I suppose I'll go and warm up.

00:12:32.480 --> 00:12:34.770
No, not yet.

00:12:34.770 --> 00:12:36.440
It's still too early.

00:12:37.940 --> 00:12:39.360
What's the meaning of this?

00:12:43.550 --> 00:12:44.610
Ball three!

00:12:47.750 --> 00:12:50.540
<i>The count is three balls... He's cornered.</i>

00:12:52.220 --> 00:12:54.500
He won't be lured by three balls, huh?

00:12:55.550 --> 00:12:58.000
<i>Why isn't the bench saying anything?</i>

00:12:58.940 --> 00:13:01.420
<i>It's impossible for Shigeno to continue.</i>

00:13:05.050 --> 00:13:06.020
Out!

00:13:06.560 --> 00:13:07.090
Out!

00:13:08.410 --> 00:13:09.300
Out! Out!

00:13:09.300 --> 00:13:09.970
Out! Out!

00:13:09.970 --> 00:13:13.390
T-Triple play?

00:13:13.390 --> 00:13:16.560
Ouch! It hurts!

00:13:16.560 --> 00:13:17.620
W-What a guy!

00:13:17.620 --> 00:13:19.480
W-What a guy!

00:13:20.330 --> 00:13:24.060
Doing a thing like that! What would you've done if you had hurt your hand!?

00:13:24.060 --> 00:13:26.800
I've gained some respect for you, samurai boy.

00:13:26.800 --> 00:13:28.450
You got some kind of problem?

00:13:28.910 --> 00:13:31.040
He's telling you that he has gained some respect for you.

00:13:31.950 --> 00:13:33.750
Oh? Was that it?

00:13:33.750 --> 00:13:35.910
Thank you, Bolton-chan.

00:13:36.790 --> 00:13:39.390
<i>This guy's fighting spirit is the real deal.</i>

00:13:40.600 --> 00:13:41.550
<i>But...</i>

00:13:41.550 --> 00:13:45.800
<i>the Majors isn't so easy that you can battle with just fighting spirit.</i>

00:13:47.610 --> 00:13:49.730
<i>Shigeno, who was so timid, is fighting this hard...</i>

00:13:49.730 --> 00:13:53.770
<i>I have to do my best too!</i>

00:13:56.250 --> 00:13:57.890
Strike out!

00:14:08.740 --> 00:14:10.070
Strike out!

00:14:14.110 --> 00:14:16.010
<i>Batting, number 30...</i>

00:14:16.560 --> 00:14:19.540
<i>Shigeno is starting to get tired, as expected.</i>

00:14:23.300 --> 00:14:24.000
Out!

00:14:25.110 --> 00:14:26.670
Just one more.

00:14:35.330 --> 00:14:36.270
Safe!

00:14:37.390 --> 00:14:40.510
You really can't lower your guard in the Majors.

00:14:51.310 --> 00:14:53.100
<i>Shigeno is at his limit.</i>

00:14:53.100 --> 00:14:55.370
<i>Why isn't the boss subbing him out?</i>

00:14:55.370 --> 00:14:58.640
<i>Get a good taste of this, Shigeno.</i>

00:14:58.640 --> 00:15:01.290
<i>The wall of the Majors starts here.</i>

00:15:16.800 --> 00:15:18.450
Has it been carved into you yet?

00:15:18.450 --> 00:15:21.620
That your samurai style will only take you this far.

00:15:22.810 --> 00:15:24.230
S-Shigeno!

00:15:28.340 --> 00:15:30.110
You're going to sub for him now, right?

00:15:30.110 --> 00:15:31.280
Not yet.

00:15:31.280 --> 00:15:32.710
Coach!

00:15:32.710 --> 00:15:35.610
I'll have Shigeno continue pitching until this inning is over.

00:15:35.610 --> 00:15:39.600
B-But, it's obvious that Shigeno is already at his limit.

00:15:39.600 --> 00:15:41.290
Even if you allow Shigeno to continue pitching...

00:15:41.930 --> 00:15:45.630
An exhibition game isn't something that you need to win, after all.

00:15:48.520 --> 00:15:53.280
<i>Most likely he'll be forced to drop down to the Minors after this game.</i>

00:15:53.280 --> 00:15:57.530
<i>However, the reality of the Majors he'll have learned through this experience...</i>

00:15:57.530 --> 00:16:02.230
<i>will become a guidepost, surpassing a million words of coaching.</i>

00:16:03.750 --> 00:16:06.690
<i>I have a feeling that this has happened to me before.</i>

00:16:06.690 --> 00:16:11.070
<i>When was it again?</i>

00:16:19.300 --> 00:16:21.260
Shigeno!

00:16:21.990 --> 00:16:23.190
Hey, Shigeno!

00:16:23.190 --> 00:16:24.040
Are you listening?

00:16:24.600 --> 00:16:27.300
This will most likely be my last inning.

00:16:27.300 --> 00:16:29.960
Then... it might be a good idea to try that.

00:16:29.960 --> 00:16:30.880
What?

00:16:31.580 --> 00:16:33.240
It's nothing.

00:16:33.240 --> 00:16:35.890
Well then, our customer has arrived.

00:16:39.520 --> 00:16:41.100
<i>I sympathize with you.</i>

00:16:41.100 --> 00:16:43.170
<i>I don't know what the circumstances are, but...</i>

00:16:43.170 --> 00:16:48.770
<i>I pity you stepping on the Major League mound with nothing but a fastball of that level.</i>

00:16:51.940 --> 00:16:53.570
<i>Shigeno, it's just as you said.</i>

00:16:53.570 --> 00:16:55.700
<i>Shigeno, it's just as you said.</i>

00:16:55.700 --> 00:16:58.000
<i>It's still too early for us to be in the Majors.</i>

00:17:00.200 --> 00:17:01.300
<i>He's... smiling!</i>

00:17:01.300 --> 00:17:02.580
<i>He's... smiling!</i>

00:17:03.320 --> 00:17:06.250
<i>It took me this long to realize it, but...</i>

00:17:06.250 --> 00:17:13.620
<i>the color of the sky in both Japan and America-
No, from my childhood too, it hasn't changed.</i>

00:17:14.660 --> 00:17:15.980
<i>And also,</i>

00:17:15.980 --> 00:17:17.760
<i>neither have I.</i>

00:17:18.180 --> 00:17:21.470
<i>Let's go, Shimizu! Miracle ball G three five!</i>

00:17:21.470 --> 00:17:23.930
<i>No way! I never heard anything about that before!</i>

00:17:24.280 --> 00:17:26.660
<i>This is... my secret weapon!</i>

00:17:33.990 --> 00:17:35.240
Change-up?

00:17:37.850 --> 00:17:39.070
Out!

00:17:42.990 --> 00:17:45.180
Hey, that pitch...

00:17:45.180 --> 00:17:47.380
It's my trump card, my miracle ball.

00:17:47.380 --> 00:17:48.530
Miracle ball?

00:17:48.530 --> 00:17:49.420
What!?

00:17:49.420 --> 00:17:53.310
I used it since I had nothing to lose. Luckily, it worked.

00:17:53.310 --> 00:17:57.590
I used the fact that they were convinced that I only threw fastballs.

00:17:57.590 --> 00:18:01.010
That pitch... It's a secret weapon I can only use once.

00:18:02.970 --> 00:18:06.140
"Well done" is what I'd like to say, but...

00:18:06.140 --> 00:18:07.850
Yeah, I understand.

00:18:08.660 --> 00:18:10.810
I'll leave the rest up to Sanchez.

00:18:11.880 --> 00:18:13.280
<i>I'm utterly defeated.</i>

00:18:13.280 --> 00:18:16.710
<i>At least for today.</i>

00:18:36.760 --> 00:18:37.510
Yo!

00:18:38.520 --> 00:18:41.210
The beginning of the game wasn't bad, but...

00:18:41.210 --> 00:18:43.150
reality wasn't so easy.

00:18:43.150 --> 00:18:44.450
Yeah.

00:18:46.330 --> 00:18:50.030
I was just sentenced by the boss to the Minor League.

00:18:51.090 --> 00:18:54.330
Well, I'll work hard and aim for my next chance.

00:18:55.020 --> 00:18:57.860
In that case, we're in the same boat, Fox.

00:18:59.260 --> 00:19:05.990
It seems that the higher ups understand clearly that I'm not at the level of competing for a roster spot from this game too.

00:19:06.860 --> 00:19:09.960
I see... So you're going to the Minors too?

00:19:10.330 --> 00:19:11.370
However,

00:19:11.370 --> 00:19:14.390
I'm not depressed at all!

00:19:18.100 --> 00:19:23.970
I've clearly seen what form and how many steps I need to climb to get to the Majors!

00:19:24.710 --> 00:19:26.430
You've... seen it?

00:19:27.170 --> 00:19:29.060
I've made a fresh start, Fox!

00:19:32.090 --> 00:19:36.230
<i>Up till now, I've only concentrated on polishing my fastball, but...</i>

00:19:36.640 --> 00:19:40.200
<i>with just that, I can't break through the wall of the Majors.</i>

00:19:40.790 --> 00:19:45.120
<i>I don't know how far I can go, having been originally right-handed, but...</i>

00:19:46.120 --> 00:19:49.080
<i>I have to find a breaking ball that fits me!</i>

00:19:58.810 --> 00:20:01.720
Good, good! You've advanced a lot, Robert.

00:20:02.840 --> 00:20:04.590
Coach Dawson.

00:20:05.140 --> 00:20:08.810
This is Shigeno and Fox, who are going to be with the Cougars from today on.

00:20:09.300 --> 00:20:14.980
Oh, Fox, you've come back.
I thought I told you not to come back here again.

00:20:14.980 --> 00:20:18.410
Well, it was out of my hands...

00:20:18.410 --> 00:20:20.160
This one's a face I haven't seen before.

00:20:20.160 --> 00:20:25.200
Yes, he's Shigeno, a pitcher. He came from Japan and got in via the tryouts.

00:20:26.740 --> 00:20:28.120
A pitcher, eh?

00:20:29.110 --> 00:20:31.980
Might you be able to pitch today?

00:20:33.230 --> 00:20:39.580
You see, Melvin, who was going to be our starting pitcher today, has back pain and can't pitch.

00:20:39.580 --> 00:20:42.760
It would help us a lot if you could fill the empty hole.

00:20:43.250 --> 00:20:46.420
It seems that he wants you to be the starting pitcher in today's game.

00:20:46.420 --> 00:20:47.630
Me?

00:20:48.230 --> 00:20:50.730
Even if the coach is saying that, you better not.

00:20:50.730 --> 00:20:54.090
You threw a lot yesterday and this morning and have to be tired, right?

00:20:54.090 --> 00:20:57.150
Oh, okay! All right, Boss!

00:20:57.150 --> 00:20:59.520
Oh, you'll do it, eh?

00:20:59.520 --> 00:21:00.890
S-Shigeno!

00:21:00.890 --> 00:21:02.640
I'm not tired.

00:21:02.640 --> 00:21:05.700
And other than that, I've figured out a couple of hard ones,

00:21:05.700 --> 00:21:08.400
and I want to try them out before I forget the feeling.

00:21:18.920 --> 00:21:20.050
Out!

00:21:21.340 --> 00:21:23.430
Put your spirit into it, you guys!

00:21:23.430 --> 00:21:26.800
Today is Shigeno's first time on the mound with the Cougars, after all.

00:21:31.520 --> 00:21:33.140
<i>They can't really be compared.</i>

00:21:34.170 --> 00:21:39.110
<i>After all, everything is really different from the flashy Majors.</i>

00:21:46.760 --> 00:21:50.250
<i>If you're the catcher, I can feel at ease.</i>

00:21:50.250 --> 00:21:52.830
<i>Shigeno, will it really be all right?</i>

00:21:52.830 --> 00:21:58.080
<i>I'm telling you it's all right.
Other than that, let's confirm them, just to be safe.</i>

00:21:59.100 --> 00:22:01.750
<i>What do you want to confirm this late?</i>

00:22:01.750 --> 00:22:07.890
<i>Isn't it obvious? The signs to the pitcher for breaking balls.</i>

00:22:08.480 --> 00:22:12.310
<i>Breaking balls? Will he really be able to throw those?</i>

00:22:12.760 --> 00:22:13.670
Play!

00:22:15.650 --> 00:22:21.190
<i>Sorry, but I'm not planning on staying at this shabby stage for many months!</i>

00:22:21.640 --> 00:22:26.030
<i>Time to hurry up, produce some results, and rise up to the Majors!</i>

00:24:11.060 --> 00:24:14.230
I can't stay in Triple A and have my legs get dull!

00:24:14.230 --> 00:24:16.220
I'm going to compensate for the things I lack right now,

00:24:16.560 --> 00:24:18.970
and get back to the mound in the Majors!

00:24:18.970 --> 00:24:20.740
Wh- You're...!

00:24:21.590 --> 00:24:22.890
Next time, on Major:

00:24:22.890 --> 00:24:24.700
I Won't Forgive You!

00:24:24.700 --> 00:24:27.270
Run to the stage of your dreams!
